## 3. DUAL-GUARD AUTHENTICATED USER CONTEXT Extraction (`auth()`)

The platform uses two guards:
- **Admin Guard (`admin`)**: Sanctum tokens for admin users (`users` table).
- **Member Guard (`member`)**: JWT tokens for portal members (`mod_membership_members` table).

### ❌ WRONG (Typehinting Concrete User Model):
```php
// VIOLATION: Hardcoding App\Models\User breaks when request originates from member portal or microservice
public function store(Request $request)
{
    /** @var \App\Models\User $user */
    $user = $request->user(); 
    $user->branch_id; // ❌ Crash on member guard or microservice
}
```

### ✅ RIGHT (Senior Authenticated Context Extraction DTO):

#### A. Auth Context DTO (`Backend/DTOs/AuthUserDto.php`)
```php
namespace Modules\Teams\Backend\DTOs;

class AuthUserDto
{
    public function __construct(
        public readonly int|string $id,
        public readonly string $name,
        public readonly string $email,
        public readonly string $guard, // 'admin' | 'member'
        public readonly ?int $branchId = null,
        public readonly array $permissions = []
    ) {}

    public static function fromRequest(\Illuminate\Http\Request $request): ?self
    {
        $user = $request->user();
        if (!$user) {
            return null;
        }

        $guard = auth()->guard('admin')->check() ? 'admin' : 'member';

