## Tier-1 Backend Security Gate — Laravel / PHP (`SEC-001..183`)
- **Deny-by-Default & Verb Safety (`SEC-016`, `SEC-050`):** Protect all non-public routes with `auth:sanctum`; forbid `Route::any` on state-mutating actions and enforce `APP_DEBUG=false` in staging/production (`SEC-086`).
- **Throttling, CSPRNG OTP & Anti-Enumeration (`SEC-021..027`):** Enforce `throttle:` middleware on login, OTP, password-reset, and bulk export routes; generate OTPs via `random_int()`, store hashed with single-use TTL + attempt caps, and return uniform responses.
- **Tenant Scope, IDOR & Mass Assignment (`SEC-036`, `SEC-039`, `SEC-040`):** Scope every query by authenticated `tenant_id` and ownership (fail-closed `404`), authorize via Policies, and declare explicit `$fillable` arrays excluding privilege/tenant/balance keys (`$guarded = []` prohibited).
- **Private Uploads & Safe Exports (`SEC-044`, `SEC-055..062`, `SEC-148`):** Store uploads, exports, and logs on private disks outside `public/`; verify server-side magic bytes via `finfo_file()`, reject active formats (`svg`, `html`, `php`, `js`), use UUID storage keys, and canonicalize paths.


## 4. Active Frontend Rules Summary

# Vue 3 UI Component Standards

- **CSS Base Enforcement:** Adhere strictly to `.ai/rules/02-frontend/vue/styling-css-base.md` based on active CSS stack (Bootstrap 5, Pure/Vanilla CSS, or Tailwind CSS).
- **Rich Text Editor Standard:** ALL rich text editing MUST use **Vue Quill Editor (`@vueup/vue-quill`)**. TinyMCE is strictly deprecated. Ensure bi-directional support (`dir="rtl"` for Arabic, `dir="ltr"` for English).
- **Predefined UI Component Reuse:** ALWAYS check for existing form components in `@components/` or `src/components/` (e.g., `<AppInput>`, `<AppSelect>`, `<AppButton>`, `<CustomFormGroup>`) and use them instead of primitive HTML `<input>`, `<select>`, or `<button>` elements.
- **Component Separation:** Keep Container Pages (`views/` or `@pages/`) separate from Presentational UI Components (`components/`).
- **API Service Layer:** Isolate all HTTP API requests inside dedicated service modules (`src/services/api/` or `@api/`). Zero direct `axios`/`fetch` calls inside presentational components.
- **Script Setup:** Use `<script setup>` for all Vue 3 components.
- **Theme & Locale Integration:** Every component MUST render smoothly across both `light` and `dark` themes and consume localized string tokens via `$t('key.path')` / `i18n.global.t('key.path')`.
- **QA Testability Locator Standard:** EVERY interactive or state-bearing element (forms, inputs, selects, buttons, modals, tabs, dynamic rows) MUST include deterministic `data-testid="{module}-{component}-{element}"` (e.g. `data-testid="memberships-form-submit"`, `:data-testid="\`memberships-row-${item.id}\`"`) per `006-qa-testability-and-handoff.md`. Never rely on CSS classes or translated text for test selectors.


# Vue 3 HMVC / Feature Module Architecture Protocol

When `architecture.hmvc == true`, frontend features are organized into self-contained **Mini-Apps** located in `src/modules/{module-name}/` (or `resources/js/modules/{module-name}/`), mirroring the primary `src/` (or `resources/js/`) folder structure:

## 1. Directory Structure per Frontend Module (Mini-App Package)
```
src/modules/{module-name}/
├── assets/                  <-- Module-specific CSS/images/icons
├── components/              <-- Module presentational UI components
├── composables/             <-- Module custom Vue composables/hooks
├── pages/ (or views/)       <-- Module container pages/views
├── router/                  <-- Module route definitions (routes.ts or index.ts)
├── services/                <-- Module API HTTP service layer
└── store/                   <-- Module Pinia store state management
```

## 2. Module Registration & Isolation Rules
- **Component Scope:** Presentational UI components specific to this module live inside `src/modules/{module-name}/components/`.
- **Global Base Component Reuse:** Base components like `<AppInput>`, `<AppSelect>`, `<AppButton>` are imported from global `@/components/`.
- **Router Integration:** Export module route array from `src/modules/{module-name}/router/` and automatically register it into the primary router instance.
- **State Management:** Keep Pinia stores scoped inside `src/modules/{module-name}/store/`.



# Vue 3 Localization Protocol (vue-i18n)

- **Initialization Standards:** `vue-i18n` MUST be initialized with `legacy: false` and `globalInjection: true` to support Composition API (`<script setup>`).
- **Safe Translation Helpers:** Use `i18n.global.t('key.path')` or `$t('key.path')` safely across components and setup scripts without legacy mode syntax errors.
- **Locale Synchronization:** Place translations in `lang/en.json` and `lang/ar.json`. ALWAYS synchronously update both Arabic and English translation files when adding/modifying UI labels, placeholders, titles, or messages.
- **RTL / LTR Text Direction:** Ensure proper document and container direction attributes (`dir="rtl"` for Arabic, `dir="ltr"` for English) across views and rich text editors.
- **Zero Hardcoded Strings:** Never hardcode user-facing strings directly in template markup.


# Vue 3 State Management (Pinia)

- **State Management:** Use Pinia stores for global state, auth tokens, and persistent user profiles.
- **Store Structure:** Define stores using composition API syntax (`defineStore('name', () => { ... })`).
- **Persistence:** Use plugin-based persistence for auth and user settings where required.


## 5. DevOps, OpenAPI & BCAS Workflow Index

1. **OpenAPI & Postman Standards:**
   - Zero inline annotations in PHP files (`@OA\` prohibited); maintain modular JSON OpenAPI specs in `docs/modules/`.
   - Run `node bin/build-postman.js` to generate Postman v2.1 collection with automatic token/resource chaining.
2. **Tracked Seeders:**
   - Seeders must be tracked in `seeder_log` / `seed_history` to ensure deterministic zero-downtime execution.
3. **Governed Workflow Commands (`v4.2.2` — `BA_AI_SDLC v2.1.0` Multi-Intake Hub, Legacy BCAS & 183-Control Pentest Gate):**
   - `@reverse-intake`: Export `REVERSE_INTAKE_BUNDLE.json` + `REVERSE_INTAKE_REPORT.md` via `node bin/reverse-architect.js --export-ba-intake` (`prototype-code` / `brownfield-cr`).
   - `@bcas-init` / `/bcas-init`: Sync `BA_AI_SDLC v2.1.0` `project-context-hub/` (`UX_DESIGN_BRIEF.md`, `_intake/`, `PARTIAL_JIT_ANCHOR`) & cascade map/DAG/radar.
   - `@review-spec [FeatureID]`: Two-Gate sealer (`READY_FOR_DEV -> READY_TO_CODE`) populating Section 11 (`ENG-01..ENG-10`, `--populate-hints`) & verifying `feature_srd` via `node bin/eng-gate.js`.
   - `@pmtool-sync [SprintID]`: Decompose `§1B` Stories (`STR-*`) into department tasks (`TSK-*-{BE,WEB,MOB,QA}`) & export PMTool `.csv`/`.xlsx` boards via `node bin/pmtool-board-sync.js`.
   - `@implement [FeatureID]`: Mode 0 1-Gate fast-track blueprint -> code consuming `SEED-*`, `ENUM-*`, Archetype `5A/5B`, and §2/§3 `data-testid`.
   - `@apply-delta [Version]`: Compile & execute `Was -> Current` deltas via `node bin/delta-sync.js`, re-handoff Mobile/QA, and mark applied.
   - `@handoff [Module]` & `@cycle-handoff`: Compile Postman v2.1, Integration Guide, and `CYCLE-*_HANDOFF.md` (`MB-01..15`).
   - `@pentest` & `@audit-security`: Run 183-Control GRC Release Gate (`node bin/pentest-suite.js --strict`), Offensive Postman DAST (`node bin/build-pentest-postman.js`), & Security Fuzzer (`node bin/security-fuzzer.js --strict`).
   - `@predict-perf`: Run Performance Predictor (`node bin/perf-predictor.js`).

> *(Refer to scoped files in `.agents/rules/`, `.cursor/rules/`, and `rules/` for exhaustive rule texts)*
